xt:** None\n*   **Errors and Warnings:** None\n*   **Likely Issue Category and Severity:** Unknown\n*   **Observed Facts vs Inference:**\n    *   **Observed Facts:**\n        *   The page has a white background with black text and a blue button.\n        *   The top-left corner has a logo that says \"CoreID\" in white text, with \"Admin Console\" written below it.\n        *   To the right of the logo is a navigation menu with the following options: \"Dashboard\", \"Tickets\", \"Users\", \"Reports\", and \"Settings\".\n        *   Below the navigation menu is a large white box with the title \"Reset Password - J. Employee\" in black text.\n        *   Inside the box is a temporary password field with the text \"Tq7#mVr2!IkJp9x\" and a checkbox next to it that says \"Force change at next sign-in\".\n        *   At the bottom of the box is a blue button that says \"Generate Temporary Password\".\n    *   **Inference:**\n        *   The user is trying to reset their password for the \"CoreID\" application.\n        *   The temporary password is \"Tq7#mVr2!IkJp9x\".\n        *   The user has the option to force a password change at the next sign-in.\n*   **Confidence Score and Notes:** CONFIDENCE SCORE: 0.95 CONFIDENCE LEVEL: High CONFIDENCE REASON: The image is clear and well-lit, making it easy to read the text and understand the layout of the page.\n\nStep 5: Temporary password relayed securely\nNavigation: Phone / voice channel — not logged in CoreID\nRead the temporary password to the caller verbally over the verified phone line. Never send it by email, chat, or ticket comment in plain text. See [CISA's guidance on requiring strong passwords](https://www.cisa.gov/secure-our-world/require-strong-passwords) for the reasoning behind credential-handling policy.\nStep 6: Ticket resolved with audit note\nNavigation: Ticketing system → ticket → Resolution notes\nLog what was done (identity checks matched, temporary password issued, force-change enabled) and set the ticket