dress, and role. The navigation menu is located on the left side of the screen and provides access to other pages in the CoreID Admin Console. The footer is located at the bottom of the screen and provides additional information about the CoreID Admin Console.\n\nStep 3: Caller identity verified\nNavigation: CoreID Admin Console → user profile → Identity Verification panel\nAsk the caller for at least 2 of: employee ID, manager's name, department, or last 4 digits of the phone on file. ✅ Do not send a one-time code to the user — your own admin session already satisfies the authentication requirement; this checklist is what verifies the caller is who they claim to be. If fewer than 2 items match, stop and escalate to your team lead rather than proceeding.\n\n### Visual Inspection Report (Image 3 (inline, following the text above)) [Confidence: 0.90 / High]:\nThe image shows a screenshot of a computer screen with a white background and a dark blue sidebar on the left side. The sidebar has a list of options, including \"CoreID Admin Console\", \"Dashboard\", \"Tickets\", \"Users\", \"Reports\", and \"Settings\". \n\n*   The main content area of the page is a white box with a title that reads \"J. Employee - Identity Verification\" in black text.\n*   Below the title, there are two checkboxes: \"Employee ID matches ticket\" and \"Manager name matches ticket\".\n*   There is also a checkbox for \"Department matches record\" and another for \"Last 4 digits of phone on file\".\n*   At the bottom of the box, there is a message that says \"2 of 4 confirmed - minimum required to proceed\".\n\nThe image appears to be a screenshot of a computer screen displaying a verification process for an employee's identity. The page has a simple design with a white background and a dark blue sidebar on the left side. The main content area of the page is a white box with a title and several checkboxes. The checkboxes are used to verify different pieces of information, such as the employee's